      "reviewStatus": "needs-review",
      "translationState": "translated",
      "sourceContractHash": "a8e955a0e1dcff27f1022173b5da2698e093b2c01d2aa99952b620519443a455"
    },
    {
      "id": "sources.strength.point.3",
      "text": "The single-leg stance, push-up and wall-sit tests each show only part of physical performance; they are not tests of your personal disease risk.",
      "requiredTerms": [],
      "reviewStatus": "needs-review",
      "translationState": "translated",
      "sourceContractHash": "fd95bfaf6950c0431f03f049aae64cb39a2a1f945831e020fb75fb605568b438"
    },
    {
      "id": "sources.strength.point.4",
      "text": "From age 18, a harmonised training guide is used for the bilateral wall sit; it is not a clinical norm or diagnostic threshold. A maximal test can cause a marked acute rise in blood pressure.",
      "requiredTerms": [],
      "reviewStatus": "needs-review",
      "translationState": "translated",
      "sourceContractHash": "6032bfd65f56b4b5b6127ec18adab2431542422cfb5fa3d430cc4a7c3d116f89"
